I work with the SAS macro language, which is very similar to the LaTeX macr=
o expansion language. In that language, the scope (global vs local vs local=
ly - global) is governed by a symbol status table, which is centrally defin=
ed. The status of the variable can be queried and defined, the status of th=
e variable is defined by its first reference, and the default is local. In =
that way, much is quite similar to the LaTeX approach. The main difference =
is that there is a master symbol table which contains the status of all var=
iables.=0A=0A=0A=A0=0APaul Thompson =0A=0A=0AProfessor and Senior Scientist=
